TI  - Evaluating Language Model Agency Through Negotiations
AU  - Tim R. Davidson
AU  - Veniamin Veselovsky
AU  - Michal Kosinski
AU  - Robert West
PY  - 2024
T2  - International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2024)
AB  - We introduce an approach to evaluate language model (LM) agency using negotiation games. This approach better reflects real-world use cases and addresses some of the shortcomings of alternative LM benchmarks. Negotiation games enable us to study multi-turn, and cross-model interactions, modulate complexity, and side-step accidental evaluation data leakage. We use our approach to test six widely used and publicly accessible LMs, evaluating performance and alignment in both self-play and cross-play settings. Noteworthy findings include: (i) only closed-source models tested here were able to complete these tasks; (ii) cooperative bargaining games proved to be most challenging to the models; and (iii) even the most powerful models sometimes "lose" to weaker opponents.
